<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $25.68 bln on Mar 28.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $25.68 bln on Mar 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $25.68 billion on March 28, 1997 from $25.14 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Mar 28	Mar 21	 Mar 29</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     21,699	21,160	 17,046</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,977	 3,977	  4,659</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2	     82</p>
<p>    Total			     25,678	25,139	 21,787</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
